        (S_MM_ORG, "Auto-Organize"),
        (S_MM_TIP_ORG, "Fills the whole chain from Merit, best first.\nYour Commander-in-Chief stays. At most {1} officers\nunder each officer; everyone else and the animals\nare spread evenly under the lowest officers.\nPeople who never fought are left out.\nUndo takes it back."),
        (S_MM_DD_CHAIN, "Order: the whole chain bodyguards its superior"),
        (S_MM_DD_CHAIN_STOP, "Order: the whole chain stops bodyguarding"),
        (S_MM_HELP, "MILITARY MANAGER (Shift+M): the chain of command you set up yourself. It comes with PZA Service Record. The chart: the Commander-in-Chief on top, then one column per unit, each led by an officer. Under every officer: a line with their Privates and their war animals, the officers below them, and empty slots (\"+ Captain\", \"+ Sergeant\"). Every box is a drop-down list: click it, scroll with the mouse wheel, pick a name. Click an empty slot to choose who takes that post. Click an officer to replace them or take them off the post: the newcomer keeps their superior and their people. Click \"Privates\" or \"Animals\" to add or remove members; one line adds everyone you have selected in the game. \"-\" or a double click on the title shrinks the window to a small button you can drag. Every list shows the people selected in the game first, then the people of that officer's own squad, then everyone not placed yet, then the rest. Search: type part of a name and every list shows only the names that contain it. Animals hold no post. There is one Commander-in-Chief: a new one makes the old one a General under them. A superior always holds a higher post. The marks: three chevrons Sergeant, two bars Captain, four stars General, five stars Commander-in-Chief. Undo and Redo take back or put back the changes made here. Hover over a name for its full line. Posts need no earned rank and squads stay as they are. Everything is saved with each character. Orders: the Privates and Animals lists start with \"Order: all bodyguard this officer\", which gives each of them Kenshi's own Bodyguard job with the officer as its target (you see it in their job list and can remove it there), and \"Order: stop bodyguarding\", which removes every Bodyguard job they hold. Officers show their portrait, and the squad portraits at the bottom of the screen carry the post mark. AUTO-ORGANIZE (button at the top): one press fills the whole chain from Merit, best first. The Commander-in-Chief you set stays; with none, the best fighter takes it. At most 5 Generals, 5 Captains under a General and 5 Sergeants under a Captain (MMOrgCap in the ini); a lower level only opens when the one above is full. Everyone else and every animal is spread evenly under the lowest officers, with no limit. Animals hold no post. People who never fought are left out: add them by hand. Undo takes the whole press back; after it you can change any post by hand. CHAIN ORDER: the Commander-in-Chief's own list has \"Order: the whole chain bodyguards its superior\" (Generals guard the Commander-in-Chief, Captains their General, Sergeants their Captain, Privates and animals their officer) and the order that stops it. An officer who leads other officers shows no Privates and Animals lines unless someone is still in them."),
        (S_HELP_INTRO, "PZA Service Record keeps every fighter's combat record and saves it with the game."),
        (S_HELP_FIGHTER, "Fighter: everything recorded for one character. It opens on the character whose stats (STA) you looked at last; Back and Next step through your squad, \"STA\" jumps back to that character."),
        (S_HELP_CHART, "THE CHART (Fighter page): the fighter's style in six axes. Each axis is measured against the best in your squad: the squad's best on an axis touches the edge, half way out is half as good, a dot near the centre is none.\n- Lethality: kills per fight.\n- Takedowns: knockouts dealt per fight.\n- Maiming: limbs taken off enemies per fight.\n- Damage: damage dealt per fight.\n- Endurance: damage taken per time knocked out (how much it takes to drop them). Someone never hit nor knocked out has no data here yet: the label is grey with a dash and the axis isn't scored.\n- First strike: one-hit knockouts and one-hit kills per fight.\nA fight is a battle that got an After-Action Report; every one of your people in it counts it (\"Fights counted\"). Fights are counted from version 0.6.8 on, and per fight means only what happened since then, so an old record isn't split over one fight. Until a fighter has a counted fight, the chart shows career totals and says so under it. Hover a label for the number, the squad best and who holds it; hover the chart for all six."),
        (S_HELP_SQUAD, "Squad: your squad as a table, best first; animals' names are ^alavender^n. The Sort button changes the column: kills, knockouts, damage dealt, biggest hit, damage taken, friendly fire."),
        (S_HELP_RECENT, "Recent: this session's knockouts, kills, limbs and friendly fire involving your people, in the order they happened (the latest on the last page). Friendly fire shows in ^ggreen^n."),
        (S_HELP_REPORTS, "Reports: an After-Action Report for each battle, written when the fight ends (30 seconds without a blow): who opened it, who held the line, who carried it, friendly fire, and what happened after. Back and Next step through the battles; the Advice button shows or hides a Sustain / Improve section in every report (off by default)."),
        (S_HELP_RANKS, "RANK (earned): every fighter earns a rank from their own record, shown by name on the Fighter page. Merit = kills x 3 + knockouts dealt x 2 + limbs taken x 2 + fights counted + damage dealt / 250; friendly fire earns nothing. The ranks: Recruit (0), Scrapper (10), Blade (30), Veteran (70), Blooded (140), Hardened (260), Champion (450), Legend (750). A rank changes nothing in the game."),
        (S_HELP_COMMAND, "CHAIN OF COMMAND: posts and who leads whom are set in the PZA Military Manager window, which comes with Service Record: press Shift+M. It has its own help page. The Fighter page shows a fighter's post, the Squad page shows it after the name."),
        (S_HELP_ARCHIVE, "Kept reports: this window shows the battles of this session only, but every report is also kept in a text file, one per faction, in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kenshi\\PZAServiceRecord\\reports (each starts with the save it was written in). Report numbers carry on from the last kept report. A report is about 3 KB. PZAServiceRecord.ini: ReportArchive=0 turns this off; ReportArchiveMaxMB (50) caps the folder, and at the cap nothing more is written."),
        (S_HELP_TIMES, "Times: \"1:23\" is the time since you loaded the game, at the game's speed (paused time doesn't count); a battle's length and when each person went down use it. Next to it, in brackets, Kenshi's own clock: \"1:23 (07:41)\". Each report's title has the Day it happened, and its first lines say \"In game: Day 413, 07:40 to 07:52\". The Recent page shows both: \"[1:23 | Day 413, 07:41]\". If the Day is one off from the game's own, change GameDayOffset in PZAServiceRecord.ini."),
        (S_HELP_NAMES, "Names and places: a report names the enemy by its kind (\"Boneyard Wolves\"), or by its faction when they come in several kinds (genin, chunin and jonin are \"Swamp Ninjas\"). In a town of theirs it is \"Our assault on\" that town; in one of your outposts, their raid; in the open, \"Our attack\" when your side struck first. A \"Where:\" line names the town."),
        (S_HELP_COLOURS, "Colours: ^ggreen^n friendly fire, ^rred^n one of ours down, ^ygold^n the leader falls or who carried it, ^oorange^n big plays, ^bblue^n defence, ^dgrey^n what came after and who never touched the enemy."),
        (S_HELP_CREDIT, "How credit works: a kill goes to the last character who hit the victim before it died; if it dies more than 10 game minutes after its last hit, it died of wounds and nobody gets the kill. A knockout goes to the hit that dropped the victim. Hitting your own side is friendly fire: it is counted on its own and never as kills or knockouts. Someone already lying down when first seen (for example after loading a save) is not a new knockout."),
        (S_HELP_KEYS, "Shift+R opens and closes this window. \"-\" (or a double-click on the title) shrinks it to a small button you can drag; mouse wheel over it for opacity. F7 hides it with Kenshi's interface."),
        (S_MEITOU_HELP_COMMAND, "CHAIN OF COMMAND: posts and who leads whom come from the PZA Military Manager. Its window is not in the Meitou version yet. Posts already in the save show on the Fighter page, and after the name on the Squad page."),
        (S_MEITOU_HELP_LANGUAGE, "Language: the window follows Meitou's own language (English, Russian, Chinese or Japanese); the Language setting on Meitou's Settings > Mods page picks another. A change needs a game restart. The After-Action Reports are in English for now."),
        (S_HELP_LANGUAGE, "Language: the window follows Kenshi's own language (English, Russian, Chinese or Japanese); Language=en in PZAServiceRecord.ini keeps it in English. A change needs a game restart. The After-Action Reports are in English for now."),
    ];
